forms very slowly, if at all, on trimmed stones that are stored in a dry, sheltered place.\n- This option weakens the argument because it suggests that the organic matter could have formed much more recently than 1,000 years ago. If rock varnish forms very slowly or not at all in certain conditions, then the organic matter beneath the varnish might not be as old as initially thought. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
