essary for the argument to hold. The argument only mentions that a 25% increase in the number of visits to the school nurse was reported, which could be due to various reasons unrelated to the decrease in air humidity.\n\nD) At least some of the visits to the school nurse after the system was modified were due to illness.\n- This assumption is necessary for the argument to hold. The argument states that a decrease in humidity can make people ill, and the 25% increase in the number of visits to the school nurse after the system was modified is evidence of this. Therefore, it is necessary to assume that at least some of the visits to the school nurse after the system was modified were due to illness.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is D) At least some of the visits to the school nurse after the system was modified were due to illness.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
