unters.\n- This option aligns with the context, which mentions that the house existed for more than 10,000 years and is at least 500 years earlier than the oldest house previously found in Britain. This suggests that the people who lived in the house had a relatively stable address, which supports the point of view.\n\nC) Humans are gregarious animals, and there are more wooden houses waiting to be discovered nearby.\n- This option is speculative and not supported by the context. The context only mentions the discovery of one house, and there is no information about other houses or the gregarious nature of humans.\n\nD) Only when ceremonial activities are held will the ornaments of processed antlers appear.\n- This option is also speculative and not supported by the context. The context only mentions the discovery of ornaments of processed antlers, but it does not provide any information about the purpose or context of their discovery.\n\nBased on the analysis, option B best supports the point of view presented in the context.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
