rcent of the material covered in anthropology, which means this statement contradicts the given information.\n\nB) The proposed area studies department would not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in any existing department other than anthropology.\n- This statement claims that the proposed area studies department would not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in any existing department other than anthropology. Since the context only mentions the Anthropology Department, this statement is not directly supported by the given information.\n\nC) The field of area studies has fewer than 50 people per year available for hire.\n- This statement claims that the field of area studies has fewer than 50 people per year available for hire. However, the context states that the proposed department will not be funded if there are fewer than 50 people per year available for hire in that field. Since the proposed area studies department will be funded, this statement contradicts the given information. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
